INTRODUCTION

*Work is mostly local
Most version control work happen in the local repository

*There is two type of repositories
-Local: Hosted pn a team member’s computer
-Remote: Hosted on a sever accessible to everyone in the team.
Mainly used to share data with others

*Features
They both have branches, commits, tags,…
The local repository includes a working copy
The remote repository contains only the git folder

*How to create  a  remote repository
by cloning a local repository using the —bare option
Or by using git int —bare command

 CONNECTING A REMOTE REPOSITORY
 A repository  cloned from a server is automatically saved by git and called “origin” but if it started with a fresh local repository , no remote connections are saved . Many remote can be connected with a local repository .

